# rust_test execution wrapper. Bazel hands a test binary two things purely
# through the environment that a libtest binary cannot read on its own, so
# stock rules_rust 0.70.0 silently ignores both:
#
#   * TESTBRIDGE_TEST_ONLY — `bazel test --test_filter=…` is accepted and then
#     does nothing; the whole suite runs and reports PASSED, which is worse
#     than an error because it looks like the filter worked.
#   * TEST_SHARD_INDEX / TEST_TOTAL_SHARDS / TEST_SHARD_STATUS_FILE —
#     `shard_count` silently re-runs the full suite N times.
#
# The patch runs every rust_test through a small wrapper that translates both
# into libtest arguments (filter → positional substring filter; sharding →
# `--list` + partition + `--exact`), composes them (the filter is applied
# during enumeration, so shards partition the filtered set), and fails loudly
# on every path where it cannot honour the request rather than reporting a
# green run that executed something other than what was asked for.
# Sharding remains opt-in behind `experimental_enable_sharding` (backport of
# rules_rust#3774); `--test_filter` support is unconditional.
# See docs/investigations/rust-test-sharding-engine-lib-test.md.
single_version_override(
    module_name = "rules_rust",
    patch_strip = 1,
    patches = ["//third_party/patches:rules_rust-0.70.0-test-wrapper.patch"],
    version = "0.70.0",
)

